<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Svartdalen: Torfinnsbu–Gjendebu — Torfinnsbu through Svartdalen to Gjendebu [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Torfinnsbu in Jotunheimen, follow the marked course through Svartdalen, cross the first eastern Storåe bridge and continue to Gjendebu. Plan about 14.5 km and 6.5 hours, with approximate climbing figures. Verify the seasonal Torfinnsdøla bridge, whose current installation is unknown, and arrange boat connections and hut dates before departure. Regular 2026 Bitihorn service ended on 13 September. Use snow-free conditions and account for boulders, high streams and poor visibility.

© Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; TurOgFriluftsruter / Nasjonal database for turruter; contributing maintainer: DNT | DNT Oslo og omegn. CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Changes: complete original walking records transformed from EPSG:25832 to longitude/latitude; only identical shared endpoint repetitions removed. Terrain-derived descent: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; DTM 10 Terrengmodell (UTM33), CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Source: https://kartkatalog.geonorge.no/metadata/dddbb667-1303-4ac5-8640-7ec04c0e3918. Changes: terrain sampled along the complete walking course at intervals of at most 10 m, centered 25 m smoothing, cumulative descent rounded to 10 m. Terrain elevation samples do not supply the walking geometry. Planning estimate: approximately 620 m descent, with tens of metres of uncertainty from the historical DTM10 model (last updates in 2013), 10 m grid resolution and differences at bridges and hut grounds. This is not a new field survey or a directly published descent measurement. The seasonal Torfinnsdøla bridge installation is currently unknown. Regular 2026 Bitihorn service ran 26 June–13 September and has ended; verify future bridge installation, boat connections and hut dates before departure. This centerline is planning only, not navigation-grade.

